{"availability":"available","full":"causewaygt/uk-heatsplit","name":"uk-heatsplit","description":"Live record of how the UK's heat and cool is delivered with a special note on geothermal","category":"Other","language":"HTML","stars":1,"forks":1,"created":"2026-07-08T11:02:40Z","updated":"2026-10-07T10:36:02Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://causewaygt.github.io/uk-heatsplit/","topics":[],"demo":"https://causewaygt.github.io/uk-heatsplit/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-07T11:15:13.381Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-07T11:15:13.381Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-07T11:15:13.381Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-07T11:15:13.381Z","stars":1,"forks":1}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Most of Britain's heat still comes from burning gas, and a material share of every unit burned never becomes useful heat. This site turns live grid data into a weekly estimate of the GB heating and cooling energy split — the energy volume, what it costs, what it emits, how much of it is UK-indigenous, who is left sweltering without cooling at all, what geothermal (deep, mine water, and ground source) supplies today and could supply next — and, at the foot of the page, why heat is the energy transition's biggest prize.","Live site: Full methodology: UK Heat Split: data sources and estimation methodology, v8 (PDF)","The page is organised as six numbered sections: 1 the starting point, 2 what heat costs and emits, 3 electricity grid impacts, 4 the rising demand for cooling, 5 UK geothermal now and next, and 6 value for money. Footnotes follow."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/causewaygt/uk-heatsplit/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"3753592df18c65649808a603c86c5a07b8f9024f37c1f34c2760f64f9c05a213","extractedAt":"2026-10-07T11:15:13.551Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-07T11:15:13.551Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Most of Britain's heat still comes from burning gas, and a material share of every unit burned never becomes useful heat. This site turns live grid data into a weekly estimate of the GB heating and cooling energy split — the energy volume, what it costs, what it emits, how much of it is UK-indigenous, who is left sweltering without cooling at all, what geothermal (deep, mine water, and ground source) supplies today and could supply next — and, at the foot of the page, why heat is the energy transition's biggest prize.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/causewaygt/uk-heatsplit/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"api_key","status":"not_required","text":"No API keys required; fork-friendly.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/causewaygt/uk-heatsplit/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"3753592df18c65649808a603c86c5a07b8f9024f37c1f34c2760f64f9c05a213","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/causewaygt/uk-heatsplit/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-07T11:15:13.552Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-07T10:36:02Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/causewaygt/uk-heatsplit/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-07T11:15:13.555Z","hash":"3753592df18c65649808a603c86c5a07b8f9024f37c1f34c2760f64f9c05a213","originalBytes":26058,"storedBytes":26058,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["cooling","heat","against","each","what","hourly","data","demand","daily","gas","geothermal","heating","what-if","energy","every","two","weekly","ecuk","hour","share","week","wind","days","docs","live","neso","three","about","anchor","annual","because","capacity","observed","own","split","cap","day","delivered","electricity","figures","four","grid","now","one","panel","published","response","source","which","window","winter","would","year","added","egec","fleet","national","rather","site","store","why","bill","britain","carbon","carries","costs","de-rated","emissions","engine","estimate","ground","history","hot","intensity","methodology","modelled","month","new","ofgem","open","per","same","solar","space","sweden","